# Namespace-based authorization with two vendors that own different namespace prefixes.
#
# - Descriptors are readable by everyone; creating or changing one requires its `namespace` to
#   start with one of the vendor's namespace prefixes.
# - Assessments are namespace-based for reads AND writes: a vendor sees only assessments in its
#   own namespace (others come back as an empty array) and is denied (403) writing outside it.
# - Any vendor may *reference* another vendor's descriptor in its own records.
#
# Credentials: the single-tenant review-variant applications (add-review-variants.ps1 output):
#   Vendor One = AssessmentVendor District  - 255901, namespace uri://one.example.com
#   Vendor Two = EdFiSandbox District       - 255901, namespace uri://ed-fi.org
# The same walkthrough works on /mt-dms/{tenant}/{schoolYear} with that tenant's variant keys.
# Re-running: creates return 201 the first time and 200 (upsert) after that.
#
# Assessment bodies carry both the Data Standard 5.2 `academicSubjects` array and the 6.1
# `academicSubjectDescriptor` field; DMS drops whichever one the deployed standard does not define.

@base = https://your-label.eastus.cloudapp.azure.com
@realm = edfi
@dms = {{base}}/st-dms

# The raw `Basic key:secret` form below is base64-encoded automatically by VS Code REST Client.
# Pre-encode it instead (`Authorization: Basic <base64(key:secret)>`) if a secret contains
# characters REST Client treats as variables ({{ }}) or your client does not auto-encode the raw form.
@oneKey = REPLACE_WITH_ASSESSMENTVENDOR_DISTRICT_KEY
@oneSecret = REPLACE_WITH_ASSESSMENTVENDOR_DISTRICT_SECRET
@twoKey = REPLACE_WITH_EDFISANDBOX_DISTRICT_KEY
@twoSecret = REPLACE_WITH_EDFISANDBOX_DISTRICT_SECRET

### Get a token for Vendor One
# @name tokenRequestOne
POST {{base}}/auth/realms/{{realm}}/protocol/openid-connect/token
Authorization: Basic {{oneKey}}:{{oneSecret}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials

###
@tokenOne = {{tokenRequestOne.response.body.access_token}}

### Use the token_info endpoint to review what this token is authorized to do (see namespace_prefixes)
POST {{dms}}/oauth/token_info
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenOne}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "token": "{{tokenOne}}"
}

### Get a token for Vendor Two
# @name tokenRequestTwo
POST {{base}}/auth/realms/{{realm}}/protocol/openid-connect/token
Authorization: Basic {{twoKey}}:{{twoSecret}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials

###
@tokenTwo = {{tokenRequestTwo.response.body.access_token}}

#
# Simple namespace demonstration, with a descriptor
#

### Use One to get academicSubjectDescriptors for uri://ed-fi.org
GET {{dms}}/data/ed-fi/academicSubjectDescriptors?namespace=uri://ed-fi.org/AcademicSubjectDescriptor
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenOne}}

### Use Two to get the same academicSubjectDescriptors
GET {{dms}}/data/ed-fi/academicSubjectDescriptors?namespace=uri://ed-fi.org/AcademicSubjectDescriptor
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenTwo}}

# These two return the same data, because everyone can read all descriptors regardless of namespace.

### Now create a new one just for Vendor One. ALLOWED.
# @name descriptor
POST {{dms}}/data/ed-fi/academicSubjectDescriptors
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenOne}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "codeValue": "codeValueOne",
  "namespace": "uri://one.example.com/AcademicSubjectDescriptor",
  "shortDescription": "description"
}

###
@descriptorUrl = {{descriptor.response.headers.Location}}

### Read it with Vendor One's token
# @name descriptorRead
GET {{descriptorUrl}}
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenOne}}

### Read it with Vendor Two's token. ALLOWED.
GET {{descriptorUrl}}
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenTwo}}

### Update it with Vendor One's token. ALLOWED (204).
PUT {{descriptorUrl}}
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenOne}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": "{{descriptorRead.response.body.id}}",
  "codeValue": "codeValueOne",
  "namespace": "uri://one.example.com/AcademicSubjectDescriptor",
  "shortDescription": "description!!!!"
}

### Update it with Vendor Two's token. DENIED (403): modifications to descriptors ARE protected by namespace.
PUT {{descriptorUrl}}
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenTwo}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": "{{descriptorRead.response.body.id}}",
  "codeValue": "codeValueOne",
  "namespace": "uri://one.example.com/AcademicSubjectDescriptor",
  "shortDescription": "description!!!!"
}

### Vendor One creates a descriptor in the wrong namespace. DENIED (403).
POST {{dms}}/data/ed-fi/academicSubjectDescriptors
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenOne}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "codeValue": "codeValueOne",
  "namespace": "uri://ed-fi.org/AcademicSubjectDescriptor",
  "shortDescription": "description"
}

#
# Writing Assessment data
#

### Vendor One creates an assessment in its own namespace, using its custom academic subject. ALLOWED.
POST {{dms}}/data/ed-fi/assessments
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenOne}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "assessmentIdentifier": "security-review-assessment-one",
  "namespace": "uri://one.example.com/Assessment/Assessment.xml",
  "assessmentCategoryDescriptor": "uri://ed-fi.org/AssessmentCategoryDescriptor#Benchmark test",
  "assessmentTitle": "Security Review Assessment One",
  "academicSubjects": [
    { "academicSubjectDescriptor": "uri://one.example.com/AcademicSubjectDescriptor#codeValueOne" }
  ],
  "academicSubjectDescriptor": "uri://one.example.com/AcademicSubjectDescriptor#codeValueOne"
}

### Vendor One creates an assessment in the uri://ed-fi.org namespace. DENIED (403): outside its prefix.
POST {{dms}}/data/ed-fi/assessments
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenOne}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "assessmentIdentifier": "security-review-assessment-two",
  "namespace": "uri://ed-fi.org/Assessment/Assessment.xml",
  "assessmentCategoryDescriptor": "uri://ed-fi.org/AssessmentCategoryDescriptor#Benchmark test",
  "assessmentTitle": "Security Review Assessment Two",
  "academicSubjects": [
    { "academicSubjectDescriptor": "uri://ed-fi.org/AcademicSubjectDescriptor#Mathematics" }
  ],
  "academicSubjectDescriptor": "uri://ed-fi.org/AcademicSubjectDescriptor#Mathematics"
}

### Vendor Two creates that assessment in its own uri://ed-fi.org namespace, referencing Vendor One's
# descriptor. ALLOWED: the assessment's namespace is checked, not the namespaces of the descriptors it uses.
POST {{dms}}/data/ed-fi/assessments
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenTwo}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "assessmentIdentifier": "security-review-assessment-two",
  "namespace": "uri://ed-fi.org/Assessment/Assessment.xml",
  "assessmentCategoryDescriptor": "uri://ed-fi.org/AssessmentCategoryDescriptor#Benchmark test",
  "assessmentTitle": "Security Review Assessment Two",
  "academicSubjects": [
    { "academicSubjectDescriptor": "uri://one.example.com/AcademicSubjectDescriptor#codeValueOne" }
  ],
  "academicSubjectDescriptor": "uri://one.example.com/AcademicSubjectDescriptor#codeValueOne"
}

### Vendor Two tries to write into Vendor One's namespace. DENIED (403).
POST {{dms}}/data/ed-fi/assessments
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenTwo}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "assessmentIdentifier": "security-review-assessment-three",
  "namespace": "uri://one.example.com/Assessment/Assessment.xml",
  "assessmentCategoryDescriptor": "uri://ed-fi.org/AssessmentCategoryDescriptor#Benchmark test",
  "assessmentTitle": "Security Review Assessment Three",
  "academicSubjects": [
    { "academicSubjectDescriptor": "uri://ed-fi.org/AcademicSubjectDescriptor#Mathematics" }
  ],
  "academicSubjectDescriptor": "uri://ed-fi.org/AcademicSubjectDescriptor#Mathematics"
}

#
# Reading Assessment data
#

### Read Vendor One's assessment with Vendor One's token. ALLOWED: the record is returned.
GET {{dms}}/data/ed-fi/assessments?assessmentIdentifier=security-review-assessment-one
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenOne}}

### Read Vendor One's assessment with Vendor Two's token. Not available: EMPTY array.
GET {{dms}}/data/ed-fi/assessments?assessmentIdentifier=security-review-assessment-one
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenTwo}}

### Read Vendor Two's assessment with Vendor One's token. Not available: EMPTY array.
GET {{dms}}/data/ed-fi/assessments?assessmentIdentifier=security-review-assessment-two
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenOne}}

### Vendor One has no claim on schools at all. DENIED (403).
GET {{dms}}/data/ed-fi/schools
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenOne}}
